   "date": "2020-01-16T21:46:29Z",
   "subject": "Changing Group Order in Multigroup CFA",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Trying to compare 4 age groups (11, 12, 13, and 14) but it is automatically fixing the age 12 group intercepts to 0 and providing analysis in the order of 12, 14, 11, 13. I want to fix the age group 11 intercepts to 0 and get the analysis in the order of 11, 12, 13, 14.<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">factor_compare </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cfa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cfs_model_01</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cfs_middle</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">equal </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;loadings&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;intercepts&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Q11&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lv </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mimic </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;mplus&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> estimator </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MLR&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor_compare</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">measures </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> standardized </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div></div><div>Brandon</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "LVjkFsvNCwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-01-17T10:42:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: Changing Group Order in Multigroup CFA",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I want to fix the age group 11 intercepts to 0 and get the analysis in the order of 11, 12, 13, 14.</div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Use the <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">group.label= </font>argument (see<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?lavOptions</font>).</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">cfa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(...,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">label </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># might need to supply a character vector instead, but probably not</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422500816000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1p-QdFOBuoy4XXwcPK38zR\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div></div></div><div><br></div><div> </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
